## Usage

Pass an adapter that binds each call to the signed-in account. The block owns the add, text-a-code, verify, and remove flow; the host owns requests, credentials, and error codes.

```tsx
import {
  AccountPhoneNumbers,
  type AccountPhoneNumbersAdapter
} from '@/blocks/account/account-phone-numbers/account-phone-numbers';

const adapter: AccountPhoneNumbersAdapter = {
  list: () => api.listPhoneNumbers(),
  add: ({ number }) => api.addPhoneNumber(number),
  sendCode: ({ number }) => api.sendPhoneVerificationCode(number),
  verify: ({ number, code }) => api.verifyPhone(number, code),
  remove: ({ id }) => api.removePhoneNumber(id)
};

<AccountPhoneNumbers adapter={adapter} identityKey={session.userId} />
```

Numbers are E.164. Throw `AccountPhoneNumbersUnavailableError` when the backend has no phone support, and an error with a `code` (or GraphQL `extensions.code`) to show the matching entry from `messages.errors`. Compose `useAccountPhoneNumbers` with `AccountPhoneNumbersView` when you need to own the layout or state.
